        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): protect ConfigurationManager mutable state with NSLock",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n`ConfigurationManager` is an `@unchecked Sendable` process-wide singleton with mutable `configuration` and `credentials` and no lock. Concurrent `loadConfiguration` / credential updates / accessors can race the dictionaries.\n\nThis PR backs both fields with an `NSLock` via locked getters/setters so existing call sites remain source-compatible.\n\n## Failure scenario\n\n1. One task reloads configuration while another reads `getAIProviders()` / credentials.\n2. Unsynchronized dictionary/struct mutation can tear or lose updates under concurrency.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `swift build --target PeekabooAutomation` → complete\n\n## Scope\n\nStorage synchronization only; precedence/parsing logic unchanged.",
